<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharafuddin of Selangor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sharafuddin Idris Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sharafuddin Idris Shah is the ninth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Selangor, who succeeded his father Salahuddin in 2001. Born in 1945, he heads one of the nine Malay royal houses whose rulers take turns to serve as Malaysia's king. As sultan he is the constitutional head of Selangor and the head of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in the state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sharafuddin-of-selangor.jpg" alt="Sharafuddin of Selangor" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Embassy Kuala Lumpur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:240830_Sultan_of_Selangor_Meeting_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
